WEBVTT

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.710
We need to inspire the people 
of Saga to rise up as one!

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.330
We'll get rid of the crooks that 
have taken control of the country!

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.070
And this time we, the samurai of Saga, will—

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.200
Yugiri-san!

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.740
Sorry to trouble you for the medicine...

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.730
How's your grandfather doing?

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.630
No real change.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.450
He spends most of the day in bed.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.120
Even though I've finally found 
a path to getting Saga back...

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:36.350
You certainly seem to 
have more comrades now.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:37.760
Yeah!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.050
We're putting together 
a petition right now...

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.730
S-See? We're gonna ask the prefectural 
magistrate to bring Saga back.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:49.550
We're even gonna go around talking 
to a bunch of the old timers from here...

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.560
That'll certainly be a big step.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:53.530
Yeah!

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.590
How are we going to accomplish anything 
if you're acting like a coward?!

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.710
You call yourself a samurai of Saga?!

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:01.320
Step outside right now! It's time 
someone beat some sense into you!

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:04.950
Th-They're just a little worked up, 
y'know... I'll go stop them.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.990
That's fine by me! It'll be a good chance 
to show you how empty your heads are!

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.430
Is that how you talk to your elders?!

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:09.000
Everyone, what's going on here?

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.530
I'm just telling the truth!

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.220
<b>Petition to the Nagasaki County Magistrate</b>

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.220
<b>In Meiji 9, Saga was abolished and integrated into Nagasaki prefecture. 
There have been a variety of problems including the management 
of communities of assorted size; supervision of agriculture, manufacture, and trade; 
and difficulties arising from reclassification of what lands belong in which prefecture.
 It is our belief that the only viable solution is to reestablish Saga prefecture.
 We humbly request the reestablishment of Saga prefecture. 
I humbly ask for your consideration on this issue.</b>

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.220
<b>October 17th, Meiji 15</b>

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.220
<b>Kiichi Momozaki</b>

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.370
Even if we have nothing else, 
we still have the future.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:30.190
A lowest point? Starting over from 
zero? That's just part of the saga.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.950
Even if we burn out in the 
process, we'll make it come true!

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.870
This is where our revenge begins!

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.370
<b>Zombie Land Saga
 Revenge</b>

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:45.660
<b>The Saga Incident, Part Two</b>

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:02.360
Damn it. How'd I get dragged into this?

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:06.670
It's fine! He offered to 
take our picture for free.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:07.530
Right.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:08.790
Nakayanagi Photography Studio

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.790
If this sample picture of us is 
enough to attract more customers,

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.770
that makes this one part of saving Saga.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.000
Or would you prefer not having your 
picture taken for some reason?

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.000
D-Don't tell me...

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.300
You think it's gonna steal 
your soul or something?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.150
Hell no!

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.910
It's fine, man! Don't worry! 
That's just a superstition!

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.180
I told you, that's not it!

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:34.550
Okay, if you could hold 
still for a second, please.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.810
Here we go.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.590
It'll make for a nice memory, if nothing else.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:41.760
Sure will!

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:47.020
I know it's a bit early, 
but how about some drinks?

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.970
Sorry, I've actually got a...

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.360
Momozaki-dono!

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.740
Maybe next time.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:55.940
See you, Yugiri-san.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:02.320
The old ruling class of Saga...

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.710
Survivors of the Saga War, I'd guess.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.870
You should watch yourself, too.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.300
What do you mean?

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.270
Those damned merchants have 
finally agreed to our demands.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.170
This should be enough to keep 
us operational for a while.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:30.270
What should we do about Momozaki-dono? 
Should we let him in on this?

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.630
Don't bother.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.370
I'm more worried about 
getting the guns in place.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:35.930
You're sure the cannons Nabeshima 
is bringing in from Tsukiji

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:38.700
will be in place to target 
the main road to Nagasaki?

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.180
Yeah, one of the merchants 
gave me his guarantee.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.080
I suppose what will be, will be.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:52.190
Kiichi is the one who accepted them 
as comrades in his efforts to save Saga.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:55.660
The world of man will always 
be shaped by the actions of men...

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.720
That's karma for you.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:10.110
Kiichi-han has been complaining that you 
haven't taken any of the medicine I sent you.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.740
There's no point. I am Saga.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.220
No, Saga is me...

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:20.250
If it's going to fade from existence,
there'll be nothing left of me, either.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:24.060
And you're convinced 
Saga's fate is set in stone,

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.450
in spite of everything 
Kiichi-han's been doing?

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.480
The heavens do favor him.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:34.260
Even now, I can see the star of Saga's 
salvation shining over him...

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:39.240
But, in the end, it will be the hands of 
men who decide matters of life and death.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:44.200
As things stand, I don't have enough 
strength to offer any real help...

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:46.060
Drink this.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.170
But... I-I just said...

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.740
Make sure to have some every day, 
until the box is empty.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.840
N-Now hang on a second!

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:19.490
No petition can ever make 
up for the anger we feel!

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:24.400
B-But we aren't trying 
to start a war here...

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.480
What we need right now, 
more than anything else, is action!

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:30.500
J-Just give me some more time, please...

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.150
I know I can get our Saga—

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.290
A boy like you can't understand!

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:41.340
What it felt like for us,
 eight years ago, seeing Saga die...

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.760
<b>Let's bring back Saga.</b>

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.760
<b>Let's return Saga to the prefecture it was before Meiji 9. 
Has living in the current Saga caused you any trouble?
 Whether it's filing official paperwork, wanting to purchase new land, 
or open a new business, contacting the prefectural office becomes necessary. 
And when there is a distance of 20 ri to said office, it becomes a major difficulty.
 When Saga was abolished, it meant the name of our homeland was lost.
 Is there any need to accept these inconveniences on top of that? 
We have endured to this day, since the fighting of Meiji 7.
 We have made personal sacrifices as a result of the outcome of that war. 
There is no need to endure any longer.
 The restoration of Saga will improve all our lives. 
The time has come to re-assess our current condition; 
to think about Saga prefecture, our homeland, and our future. 
We will take action to improve our lives.</b>

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:51.450
Isn't enough enough?

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:54.790
You did what you could,

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.900
but there's nothing but 
destruction ahead, now.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.720
The survivors of the Saga War 
are arming up again.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.480
There's no way the army ignores that.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:09.110
Everything that happened eight 
years ago is gonna happen again.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:14.450
You have to realize it by now.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:17.630
Pure idealism isn't enough 
to change the world.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:22.960
But if I back down now... 
what happens to Saga?

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.520
It'll make everyone give up.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:29.140
They'll think Saga really can't 
do anything and stop trying.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:31.680
Thinking they can't change anything...

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.730
I can't let it end like that!

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:38.750
No matter where you were born 
or what your background is,

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:42.560
Saga should be a place where people 
can do what they want to!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.730
Where you can reach for the future! 
And help each other!

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:48.310
That's the new Saga I want to bring back!

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:49.440
You need to wake up!

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.600
How long are you going to keep yelling 
about this stupid kid's dream?

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:57.810
This country is still immature... 
Twisted and barbaric.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.200
It will crush you like you're nothing!

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:03.610
Quit trying to make it sound like it's over!

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.830
Saga hasn't even begun yet!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.550
If this keeps up, 
Kiichi's going to be a fugitive.

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:04.360
He might not have meant to, 
but he helped spark a rebellion.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:07.540
You should get out of Saga for a while.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.930
I wasn't joking about what I said before.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:11.790
I think together, the two of you could—

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:12.660
Itou-han...

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:18.190
Do Kiichi-han's ambitions really 
seem that shallow to you?

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:24.480
He's seriously such an idiot.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:28.840
Awkward and bashful, but determined, 
in spite of being helpless...

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.310
That's why I...

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:34.540
Look after him for me.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:50.610
<b>To Takato Ooki-sama</b>

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.320
<b>To Shigenobu Ookuma-sama</b>

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.220
Thank you very much.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.480
Thanks!

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:21.180
<b>Izakaya</b>

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:40.740
<b>Chinzei News
New prefecture set to be established inside Nagasaki</b>

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:40.750
What we need right now, 
more than anything else, is action!

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.740
<b>Nagasaki Prefectural Office
 to Establish a New Prefectural Magistrate</b>

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:57.890
Who are you?

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:45.460
This is why I told you to stop.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:59.000
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:04.030
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:09.130
Itou... why...?

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:13.820
What are you doing? Why would you...?

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:18.260
Well, Kiichi? Does this change things? 
Still not gonna give up?

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:23.150
My job is to keep an eye 
on rebels lurking in Saga.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:26.520
It would've been fine if you had 
kept to your childish campaign.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:29.690
But once it crossed a certain line...

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:31.680
I-Itou...

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.390
This is all I have.

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:39.940
This country's still twisted and barbaric.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:45.820
Full of people like me, who don't know how 
else to live and don't have any other options.

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:49.250
Answer me, Kiichi!

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:52.900
Stop, Itou!

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:20.440
Kiichi-han!

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:36.580
People will be on our trail. 
You should leave Saga for now.

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:40.800
Why'd it end up like this...?

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:45.680
I never really understood 
what was going on...

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:49.920
But Itou... and my comrades...

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.930
Because of me! All of it!

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:55.720
I stirred all this up! Let them all die!

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.730
How am I... How am I supposed 
to make a new Saga?!

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:05.730
Please, just go.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.820
They're only after me...

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:11.060
and I don't care anymore.

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:12.580
I don't want you to—

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:17.220
I don't want to hear any whining!

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:23.030
What you're after might be a naive, 
childish dream, Kiichi-han...

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:27.160
But the fact is that was what 
got things moving again in Saga.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:30.170
You have a responsibility 
to see it through!

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:34.500
A lot of people who were inspired 
by your words have died.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:37.900
As it stands, that will all be for nothing

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.320
if you don't make your dream a reality!

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:45.400
You're going to get it back, 
aren't you? Create a new Saga?

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:49.670
Even when people mocked you, 
you had faith in that and pressed on.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:52.020
Are you going to turn your back on
all of that and act like it meant nothing?

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:05.710
Go through Mitsuse Pass, 
then take a boat from Hakata to Nagasaki.

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:09.340
The letter will tell you 
what to do from there.

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:13.810
I asked some old acquaintances 
of mine for help.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:20.400
With their support, even the government 
won't be able to lay a hand on you.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:26.520
This is all I can do for you.

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:30.230
What happens once you survive is up to you.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:36.120
Please, show me what the new 
Saga you create looks like.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.300
<i>I swear, with everything I have...</i>

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:54.840
<i>I will create a new Saga!</i>

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:14.770
Damn it, I didn't think a legendary 
courtesan would be this legendary.

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:17.750
Who the hell was the guy 
who set you free, anyway?

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:24.140
Have you ever heard the 
name "Sheathed Kichiemon"?

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:26.380
The Demon of Hibiya...!

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:33.700
I better take this seriously, then.

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:18.500
Sorry. I guess you're stuck 
with the short end of the stick.

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:20.030
Why...?

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:28.220
A place where everyone... 
can live freely, the way they want...

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:13.420
<i>By the time you are reading this letter, 
I will likely no longer be alive.</i>

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:19.100
<i>A few of my old acquaintances have 
sworn to look after Kiichi-han.</i>

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:24.730
<i>But with blood having been spilled
 and signs of rebellion growing in Saga,</i>

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:28.360
<i>someone will have to accept 
responsibility and punishment for it.</i>

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:33.390
<i>I think that this entire 
incident, and my involvement,</i>

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:35.950
<i>will all be treated like it 
never happened in the end.</i>

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:42.770
<i>If Kiichi-han asks you, 
please tell him I left Saga safely.</i>

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:47.890
<i>And, if you truly are Saga itself...</i>

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:53.010
<i>then please guide the new Saga 
that Kiichi-han creates.</i>

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:05.010
This is goodbye.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:15.670
<b>May 9th, Meiji 16 (1883)</b>

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:15.670
<b>Saga gains independence from Nagasaki thanks
 to an appeal from supporters in the prefecture</b>

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:20.180
<b>On August 4th of that year, the Military Justice Reform 
law bans unilateral executions by military personnel</b>

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:24.640
<b>On August 13th of the same year, the first Saga prefectural assembly is held</b>

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.140
<b><i>Franchouchou</i></b>

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.140
<b>The Saga Incident, live!</b>

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.140
<b>Photo ops included!</b>

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:33.130
Hey, anybody seen my hat?

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.840
You had it on during rehearsal, didn't you?

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.410
Maybe you left it somewhere.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.640
I'm telling you, I left it right here!

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.900
Tae-san, what are you chewing on?

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:42.800
Oh, no...

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:45.890
Tae-chan, no! That's not even squid!

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:49.530
Ew, it's drooly and smooshed!

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:54.090
What are you loafing around for, 
you easy breezy parcheesi zombiesees?!

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:57.250
The crowd's butts are getting 
numb waiting for you!

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:01.100
Okay, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:02.650
Come on, Yugirin!

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:03.420
Right.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:17.080
<i>Saga...</i>

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:25.180
<i>Saga!</i>

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:31.620
<i>Saga...</i>

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:34.730
<i>Yeah</i>

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.370
<i>Check it out, check it out, 
check it out, check it out</i>

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:50.270
<i>Check it out, check it out, 
check it out, check it out</i>

00:20:50.450 --> 00:20:52.810
<i>All by myself with crimson lipstick (Yeah)</i>

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.940
<i>Reapplied in the middle of the night (Yeah)</i>

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:59.040
<i>It starts to dry out as I wonder, 
are you coming tonight or not?</i>

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:03.240
<i>Tearing the petals off one 
by one (from a bellflower)</i>

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.280
<i>Feels like my patience is falling apart, too</i>

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:08.180
<i>A harlequin, kept captive</i>

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:12.010
<i>Check it out, check it out, 
check it out, check it out</i>

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:15.870
<i>Check it out, check it out, 
check it out, check it out</i>

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:18.550
<i>They say I'm friendly to everyone (Yeah)</i>

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:20.630
<i>And you know how rumors start (Yeah)</i>

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:24.760
<i>I'm ready to wallow in my sadness,
 so come and take me</i>

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:25.890
<i>When you're feeling</i>

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:26.740
<i>On top of the world</i>

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:29.070
<i>There's no way to endure 
the waves of affection</i>

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:30.170
<i>And when you're having</i>

00:21:30.170 --> 00:21:31.170
<i>A bad time</i>

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:32.500
<i>Come on over...</i>

00:21:33.760 --> 00:21:38.320
<i>You'll dance with passionate frustration like 
a butterfly (Bound up, bound up, bound up, bound up)</i>

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:43.140
<i>I want us tied together with flowing blood 
(from thorns, from thorns, from thorns, like a rose)</i>

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:44.980
<i>From Mitsuse Pass to Tawarazaka (And beyond)</i>

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:47.020
<i>Drop by to see me, even in hell</i>

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:49.050
<i>Battered by the wind and buffeted by hail</i>

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:49.720
<i>Come on by</i>

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:51.770
